text:
maya: FYI CI lint failing on helm chart for gpu-scheduler — topologySpreadConstraints rendered as null in some kustomize overlays and kubeval/helm-lint is rejecting it. Anyone seen this?
aj: repro steps? which pipeline/job?
maya: run `make chart-lint` on branch infra/helm-gpu-affinity. Fails in `helm template` -> kubeval on the eu overlay. Error: `spec.template.spec.topologySpreadConstraints: null is not of type object`
sasha: I ran into a similar one earlier with tolerations being `null` when overlay removed nodeSelector. Likely helper returning `null` instead of omitting the field.
ci-bot: build #3421 failed: helm-lint -> kubeval error at charts/gpu-scheduler/templates/deployment.yaml:line 62
maya: here's the minimal snippet from our helper that probably causes it:
```
{{- define "redwood.podSpecExtras" -}}
  topologySpreadConstraints: {{ toYaml .Values.topologySpread | nindent 2 }}
  tolerations: {{ toYaml .Values.tolerations | nindent 2 }}
{{- end -}}
```
maya: If `topologySpread` is `null` in an overlay the `toYaml` call prints `null` and the key remains, which kubeval flags.
aj: fix is to guard with `hasKey` or use the `default` helper to omit entirely when empty. I usually use a small helper: `safeToYaml` that returns empty string when nil.
philip: suggestion: update _helpers.tpl with:
```
{{- define "redwood.safeToYaml" -}}
{{- if and . (ne . "") -}}
{{ toYaml . | trim | nindent 2 }}
{{- else -}}
{{- "" -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
```
philip: then in podSpecExtras: `{{ include "redwood.safeToYaml" .Values.topologySpread }}` and only render the key when non-empty.
sasha: also double-check chart values.schema.json — CI linter (chart-testing) enforces schema and some overlays set `topologySpread: null` to intentionally remove it, which conflicts with `required`/`type` in schema. We should update schema to allow `null` or better, make overlays set `{}` instead of `null` in kustomize patches.
maya: good call. For now pushing a quick patch to helper + unit test in helm-unittest so `make chart-lint` passes. I'll open a PR.
aj: also add a helm unittest case for the eu overlay where `topologySpread` absent/null -> ensure no `topologySpreadConstraints:` shows up in rendered YAML.
ci-bot: maya created PR #1284 (infra/helm-gpu-affinity) · checks pending :github: 
maya: cc @sasha @aj @philip — will roll this into the next spike for chart lint hardening and add docs snippet for authors to prefer omitting keys over `null`. :+1:
philip: one more note — this cropping of keys interacts with our KV caching runtime tests: if nodeAffinity fields disappear entirely we can route to different GPU pools; need to validate routing tests still pass after helper change. I'll add a quick integration check in staging.
sasha: thanks — if anyone sees other `null`-leaking helpers, ping this thread and we can batch-fix. :eyes:
maya: thanks all, I'll merge after green CI.
